<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · France and the Low Countries</p><h1 class="st-title">Frisian Kingdom</h1><p class="st-meta">600 CE – 734 CE (approx.) · capital Dorestad</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Pagan kingdom of the North Sea coast, ruler of the trading port of Dorestad, which resisted the Franks for over a century.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After the Roman period the coastal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/low-countries">Low Countries</a> were resettled from the 5th century, and by around 600 the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/frisii">Frisians</a> held a realm stretching along the coast from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zwin">Zwin</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/weser">Weser</a>, later called Magna <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frisia">Frisia</a>. Its first known king, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aldgisl">Aldgisl</a>, sheltered the English <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wilfrid">Wilfrid</a> in 678.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/frisii">Frisians</a> were seafaring traders whose merchants carried cloth, slaves and goods across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-sea">North Sea</a>, and their emporium of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dorestad">Dorestad</a> on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a> was one of the busiest ports in north-west <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>. Their <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a> sceattas circulated widely. King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/redbad">Redbad</a> opposed the Christian mission of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/willibrord">Willibrord</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pippin-of-herstal">Pippin of Herstal</a> defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/redbad">Redbad</a> around 690 and took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dorestad">Dorestad</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/lordship-of-utrecht">Utrecht</a>, but Redbad recovered much ground before his death in 719. In 734 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-martel">Charles Martel</a> defeated and killed King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poppo-of-frisia">Poppo</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-boarn">Boarn</a>, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frisia">Frisia</a> was absorbed into the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-the-franks">Kingdom of the Franks</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/frisian-kingdom.jpg" alt="Frisian Kingdom" width="320" height="331"><figcaption>Image: RACM &amp; TNO; derivative work by Richardprins (... · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Frisia_716-la.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>600 CE – 734 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Dorestad</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Aldgisl, Redbad, Poppo</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Germanic paganism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Old Frisian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/netherlands">Netherlands</a>, <a href="/countries/germany">Germany</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Magna Frisia</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=667&amp;focus=frisian-kingdom" aria-label="Frisian Kingdom on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4795 378 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Frisian Kingdom lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5115 634L5054 728"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5054 728h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5115 634h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5115 634h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its capital. <a href="/atlas?year=667&amp;focus=frisian-kingdom">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

